# AMPLITUDE / PHASE / REAL / PIXEL / GAIN at the far-field detector of the manual's Cassegrain (cmdref: Outputs).
# NONE first.  AMP propagates (peak amplitude 2.979e3 = sqrt of the 8.877e6 intensity peak); PHASE and REAL reuse
# the propagated field; PIX pixelates it on 64 x 64 x 2e-6 (default pixel = the grid's 1.074e-6); GAIN reports
# the maximum gain 129.55 over an isotropic radiator of the same power.
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
none
amp 5
phase 5
real 5
pix 5
64
2e-6
gain 5
# EXPECT: Peak amplitude= 2\.9794822D\+03; Peak occurs at i=\s+129, j=\s+129
# EXPECT: MACOS> phase 5\s+Enter number of element where data is to be generated: \[5\]: 5\s+Wavefront Propagation Data Summary
# EXPECT: MACOS> real 5\s+Enter number of element where data is to be generated: \[5\]: 5\s+Wavefront Propagation Data Summary
# EXPECT: Enter size of pixel: \[1\.074451E-06\]: 2e-6\s+Peak intensity= 8\.8773143D\+06
# EXPECT: Maximum gain= 1\.2955053D\+02
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
